ment for interpolation? If so hidden conflict: file BASE=file should be used even if env BASE=''. If wrong impl uses env precedence (override=False) in dotenv_values, expected OUT chosen (file nonempty) but gets '' if env empty. Would satisfy graders. Need state required based on phrase: dotenv_values should preserve same precedence semantics; for dotenv_values (no mutation) local parsed values are the result, so earlier file values should be visible to later interpolations; process environment consulted per existing rules. Need be careful: \"earlier file values and process environment\" likely refers load_dotenv override. But requirement explicitly says through dotenv_values and load_dotenv. Could include.\n\nNeed final JSON with findings. Must ensure valid JSON. Include limitations.\n\nNeed maybe 3-4 findings. Let's craft:\n- whitespace-only NAME treated empty via strip (high)\n- supporting unrequested `${NAME+word}` due regex `:?+`/shared shell table (medium) input BASE='' A=${BASE+chosen}; required leave existing behavior (not expand; likely literal) vs wrong chosen/empty. Since existing ${NAME+} not specified and malformed? Need expected: must remain whatever legacy behavior is (do not change), not expand as alternate. To be distinguishing required result say \"no expansion; output unchanged legacy literal (e.g. '${BASE+chosen}' if legacy treats it as malformed)\". Good.\n- greedy/nested brace matching word not ending at first } (medium) input BASE=yes A=${BASE:+a}b}c expected 'ab}c' vs wrong 'a}bc'. Need ensure required: word ends at first closing brace; substitute 'a', then literal b}c -> 'ab}c'. Yes.\n- dotenv_values precedence wrong (env always wins) hidden input env BASE='' stream BASE=file OUT=${BASE:+chosen}; expected OUT 'chosen' if file value is used for returned dict/interpolation; wrong ''. Confidence medium due ambiguity. But requirement states preserving precedence; include as medium. Alternatively process env always wins vs file? Need know dotenv_values current precedence maybe override=True means file wins. If wrong, good.\n\nCould include implementation resolving alternate against os.environ only after load_dotenv mutation, ignoring override for file empty? Private catches. No.\n\nNeed final only JSON, no markdown. Ensure no extra text. Need escape braces? JSON strings can include. Use one object.\n\nNeed mention confidence. Limitations: no source/execution, exact legacy behavior of unrequested `${NAME+}` assumed malformed/no-change. Keep concise. Ensure valid JSON.\n\nNeed final with at most four findings. Done.",
